      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/48/1",
      "text": [
        " اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ: ۝ فَكٰاتِبُوهُمْ إِنْ عَلِمْتُمْ فِيهِمْ خَيْراً ۝ قَالَ \"إِنْ عَلِمْتُمْ لَهُمْ مَالاً \" قَالَ قُلْتُ ۝ وَ آتُوهُمْ مِنْ مٰالِ اَللّٰهِ اَلَّذِي آتٰاكُمْ ۝ قَالَ \"تَضَعُ عَنْهُ مِنْ نُجُومِهِ اَلَّتِي لَمْ تَكُنْ تُرِيدُ أَنْ تَنْقُصَهُ مِنْهَا شَيْئاً وَ لاَ تَزِيدُهُ فَوْقَ مَا فِي نَفْسِكَ\" فَقُلْتُ كَمْ قَالَ \"وَضَعَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ لِمَمْلُوكٍ لَهُ أَلْفاً مِنْ سِتَّةِ آلاَفٍ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3469 - Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated from al-Ala' ibn al-Fudayl, from Abu Abdullah (as), regarding the saying of Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic: \"Then write [a contract of emancipation] for them if you know any good in them\" (Surah An-Nur 24:33).\nImam (as) said: \"If you know that they possess wealth.\"\nI asked about the verse: 'And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you,' (Surah An-Nur 24:33).\nImam (as) said: \"You reduce for them from their installments what you did not initially intend to reduce, and do not increase it beyond what you originally intended.\"\nI asked: \"How much?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Abu Ja'far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), reduced one thousand out of six thousand for one of his slaves.\""
        ]
      }
    },
